## Sync classes

The set is deliberately small: every file here is dispatched by name at
runtime, or is this README. Nothing is kept "in case it is useful later" —
that is what produced a 22-file catalogue where 11 were dead (2026-08-15).

- VENDORED — taken from upstream near-verbatim; only the frontmatter tool
  restrictions are patched to this repo's role-class discipline. These are
  diffed against upstream by the refresh script; a material upstream change
  should usually be ported.

- ADAPTED — the body was rewritten for this pipeline. The upstream diff is
  INFORMATIONAL only: never bulk-apply it, or the adaptation is lost. Read it
  to notice new upstream ideas worth re-adapting.

- OURS — no upstream. Not diffed.

## Mapping (local | upstream path within its repo)

### VENDORED — VoltAgent/awesome-claude-code-subagents

  backend-developer.md  | categories/01-core-development/backend-developer.md
  test-automator.md     | categories/04-quality-security/test-automator.md
  security-auditor.md   | categories/04-quality-security/security-auditor.md

  Local patches (each carries an HTML comment near its frontmatter):
  - ALL THREE (2026-08-15, second pass) — upstream's dead inter-agent
    machinery removed: the "Query context manager" step (context-manager is
    the Discovery stage's own persona here, not a service a stage can
    query), the requesting_agent JSON protocol blocks, the canned delivery
    notifications with fabricated statistics (an open invitation to invent
    results), and the "Integration with other agents" lists naming agents
    that do not exist in this roster. Replaced with target-repo-conventions
    openings and honest-reporting instructions. A re-vendor from upstream
    would restore all of it — port upstream changes by hand.
  - backend-developer.md — additionally, upstream's "deep expertise in
    Node.js 18+, Python 3.11+, and Go 1.21+" opening removed (first pass).
    A persona dispatched for arbitrary target repos cannot carry a language
    list; the language comes from the target's own CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md.
  - security-auditor.md — tools restricted to Read, Grep, Glob (read-only
    auditor; upstream ships write access).

